WEBVTT

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.240
What is that thing?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.410
The monster.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.330
Do you know what it is?

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.500
The monster is the monster.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.000
Appears during nighttime and destroys the world.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.340
How do you know that?

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.510
<i>Haruki woke up.</i>

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.470
<i>This is the dream world's Haruki.</i>

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.760
Haruki, what happens to the world
after it gets destroyed?

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.260
I don't know.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.100
Usually it somehow goes back
to the way it used to be.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.060
What's wrong?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.440
I'm really... sleepy.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.370
Good morning.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.490
Morning.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.980
Let's assume that all of our memories are fake.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.240
Would we still be able to be here together like this?

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.860
Of course.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.950
Memory isn't reliable to begin with.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.790
As time passes, our memories get blurry,

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.500
and sometimes we're mistaken from the beginning.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.580
Still, feelings are born from those very memories.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:15.130
Even if we make mistakes,
even if we get the wrong idea,

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:21.050
the result is the same—I'm here, and so are you—
and I think just believing in that is fine.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.310
I got a present from a certain girl.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.890
She gave it to me in an absurdly roundabout way,

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.730
and put far more effort into making a perfect gift

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.730
than even something like a handmade sweater.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.940
Good for you. And?

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.730
It's just like you're saying.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.820
It doesn't matter if we make
mistakes or get the wrong idea.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.280
My feelings are born from my memories.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.290
So...

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.040
So?

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.500
I like this world.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.380
You're laughing, and all kinds
of problems disappear without a trace.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.550
It might just be the perfect answer.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.550
But I have my memories.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.510
That's why I can't stay here forever.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.930
I don't really get what you're saying.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.100
I know, I'm sorry.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.230
I wish I could explain it better.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.270
But I guess...

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.900
I guess it simply means that I was rejected?

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.490
Yes, that's exactly it.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.000
Sunday
September 24th

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.000
I couldn't meet with the old man
from the stray cat mansion in the end.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.460
He used to live in an old house,

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.880
but apparently it was demolished
and there's a parking lot there now.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:48.470
Isn't your ability useful for searching for people?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.480
I can share my senses with cats when I sleep.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.610
But if I go to sleep in the dream world,
I'll wake up in the real world,

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.820
and won't be in there anymore.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.150
Let's ask Murase for help.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.320
She can find him for sure.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.740
Will she come if we call her?

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.490
There should be a Murase
in the dream world as well.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.420
Heya, rise and shine!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.510
I just fell asleep.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.640
Tyltyl, there's someone I want to meet.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.770
Try visiting the stray cat mansion at 3 PM today.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.230
I heard it's a parking lot now.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.690
That's how it usually looks to people, yes.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.440
But there is in fact a house there.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.490
Today, from 3 PM until dusk,

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.860
it'll regain its original form.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.030
What kind of ability does the old man
from the stray cat mansion have?

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.910
His ability is to write out the text of the Script.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.830
The Script?

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:01.540
"Read volume 407 of the Script very carefully."

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.050
Let's talk another time when
we have the opportunity. Bye.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.590
Is something wrong?

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.310
I know how to find the stray cat mansion.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.360
Sumire!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.650
It's been a while, Mytyl.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.070
How've you been?

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.190
Great!

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.950
Are you going to eat?

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.950
I'll take ice cream!

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.160
I just met Tyltyl.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.490
He told me you were here.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.410
I see. Everything fine between you two?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.750
Of course!

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.960
We're Mytyl and Tyltyl after all.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.460
Say, Mytyl.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.550
Are you satisfied with your life in this world?

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.170
Of course!

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.720
There's no happier place than this world.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:52.760
I can walk, I can run, and I can eat ice cream!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.560
No matter what happens, Tyltyl will protect me.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.480
There's nothing I wish I had.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.650
<i>A sweet lemon, huh?</i>

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.030
What's wrong?

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.780
You're not yourself, Sumire.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.910
Say, aren't you meeting with the
old man from the stray cat mansion?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.910
The old man from the stray cat mansion?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.160
Yeah.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.920
The old man that just keeps writing
out the text of the Script all alone.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:24.540
Oh, I guess there was a person like that, yeah.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.050
I don't care though!

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.510
Why?

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.550
I'll go wash it!

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.520
I'd rather you not talk about
that old man with Mytyl.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.480
Why? It's possible he's what we need to save her.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.270
She's afraid of him.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.940
And I need to protect her.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.780
I see. Do whatever you want.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:00.580
It's that house.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.340
The old man from the stray cat mansion
used to live in that house.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.840
So yesterday there was a parking lot here?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.010
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.590
You aren't using the front door?

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.970
The gate is locked.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.520
There should be a hole in the wall
here that we can go through.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.230
Here. It's still usable.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:49.170
Both of you should keep in mind
that you're wearing skirts.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.800
I understand.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.140
Hi.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.560
This way.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:21.490
I'm coming in.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.000
It's been a while.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:33.260
You are...

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.470
I don't remember how many years it has been.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:41.600
Five years, eleven months, and nine days.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.310
There should be cookies in the kitchen.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.520
If you want some, you can go look for them.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:51.480
Thank you.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:01.080
I guess it's part of getting old that I'm
forgetting even where I put the cookies.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.080
But you knew the exact day you last met Nonoh?

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.960
So her name's Nonoh.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.580
You didn't know?

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.040
Names are just symbols.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.170
Symbols to differentiate between people.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.170
If you don't need to differentiate between people,
you don't need names.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:20.760
Aside from cats, she was the only
person coming to this house.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.260
I didn't need to differentiate.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.010
I see.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.270
Numbers are the only thing I never forget.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:31.230
Even if I forget where I put the cookies,
I still remember that there are thirteen of them left.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.230
Do you like numbers?

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.230
I do.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.740
Are you her friends?

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.320
I don't really classify people as friends,
acquaintances, or anything else.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.160
But if you think so,

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.330
I don't mind you calling them my friends.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.580
What are you doing in the dream world?

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.670
My lungs, kidneys, and spine are in bad shape.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.260
I can't sit properly anymore.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.840
Is your life here pleasant?

00:10:58.840 --> 00:10:59.840
It is.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:03.850
I live the same way as I used
to back when I first met you.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.560
Could you tell us about your ability?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:10.810
If I have to put it into words,
it's an ability that records the truth.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:14.060
It automatically, separately from my consciousness,

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:17.780
moves my hand and writes
down the truth in a notebook.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.110
The truth?

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:22.660
All the truth is engraved in the world.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.990
The Bureau calls it the Script.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.490
The Script...

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:31.710
My ability is to write out the text of the Script.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:35.880
The Bureau generally forbids entry to this world,

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:39.130
but thanks to my ability they allowed an exception.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:43.260
Would it be possible to read what you wrote?

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.470
They're in my office. Do as you like with them.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:47.720
A script?

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.560
Yes, a script.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.690
The gods wrote it,
and handed it to Laplace's Demon.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:56.400
However, the Demon died in 1927.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.780
Heisenberg killed it.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:03.070
Laplace's Demon died to the limitations of physics.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.280
But the abilities in Sakurada easily
break the normal laws of nature.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:10.910
With those abilities,
Laplace's Demon can be revived.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.790
And what is this script?

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:17.670
Let's assume the world is just one big stage.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.210
We're all just actors.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:23.930
We abide by the Script,
and act and talk as is written in it.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:27.430
The wind blowing, the sun rising and setting,

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.600
are all according to the Script.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.560
But this is just hypothetical, right?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.150
You're aware of the reset ability, right?

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:35.770
Yes.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:40.030
Even if the world is reset, the future stays the same.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:44.610
After a reset, people take exactly
the same actions as before it.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:45.910
All according to the Script.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:49.620
But Asai has memories from before resets.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.330
That's how he can change his actions after a reset.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:57.710
Resetting and changing the future
is regulated by the Script from the start.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:04.510
In fact, the future-seer predicts even how
the reset will be used for the nameless system.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:08.970
And her clairvoyance is also a part of the Script.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:13.680
The written copy of the Script has even recorded
the Witch's words with perfect accuracy.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:18.690
The Script stands above clairvoyance,
and accurately predicts the absolute future.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.790
This puzzle ring is about searching for what is right.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.710
How do I find what is right?

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:46.260
You need to imagine two boxes.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.430
Empty boxes, A and B.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.810
And then?

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:55.980
You put everything you can think of into A.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.560
Everything?

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.810
Yes, everything.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.690
What is there in this world?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:09.660
Cats.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.080
Those too.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.240
What else?

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.910
Me, you, my parents...

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.750
Milk, cookies.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.250
Exactly.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.340
There's also socks, clothes, the law,

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.090
lies, and Euler's formula and such.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.300
Formula?

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.930
One of the most beautiful things in this world.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:36.180
Anyway, you put everything,
all kinds of things, into that box.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:40.270
Bed sheets. Detergent. Whipped cream.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.520
Swings. The sun. The night.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:49.150
When you finish putting more or less everything
in there, you find among them what is not right

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.820
and move them to B.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.790
Don't feel bad, move them
if they're even slightly not right.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.540
Lies and socks aren't right.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.960
I understand lies, but why socks?

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.250
You can mismatch a pair.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.590
And they're dangerous if you
try to put them on while standing.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:07.590
I see.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.130
Whipped cream should be okay though.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.180
It's bad if you eat too much of it.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:15.140
And your mouth gets all sticky.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.180
Oh, right.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.180
How long should I keep doing this?

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:24.190
Until you move every single thing from A into B.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.570
Every single thing?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:30.570
Everything in this world is in some way not right.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:34.660
No matter how good,
everything has at least one bad side.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.950
Is that how it is?

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:41.330
Once you finish moving everything from A into B,

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:45.960
you now look into B and pick the least wrong thing.

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.840
That is what is right.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.430
But it's not right in some way, isn't it?

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.680
If you understand its bad sides,

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:59.140
and still think it's right,
then it's your truly right thing.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:02.350
What did you think of?

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.060
Cats.

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:09.990
And this is how you find what is right.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.500
I see... so that's how it is.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.790
That was simply luck.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:33.130
You've always lived possessed by your ability.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.260
That's true.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.050
Do you disapprove?

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:39.810
No, because I live the same way.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:43.560
This world is similar to our abilities.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:47.060
It's my fault.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:50.570
I failed to teach you what
a child should've been taught.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.700
But you saved me.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:56.200
Saved? I don't remember that.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.660
It's fine.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:01.200
There's nothing as beautiful as being saved
by someone who doesn't realize it.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.210
Do you remember the day we first met?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:10.050
Nine years, two months,
and twenty seven days ago.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:13.220
You came in here running after a cat.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.970
I asked for the cat's name.

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.350
I don't remember that, unsurprisingly.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:20.680
But I know what my answer was.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:24.270
Personally, I hate naming cats.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:25.810
I think it's very arrogant.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:30.320
But even if I feel that way,
no one else understands.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.110
You were different, though.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:35.990
It wasn't really out of respect for cats.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.530
I just find it bothersome to call them by names.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:41.870
I can't really find myself comfortable
living among humans.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:46.250
A human child who feels that way suffers a lot.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.170
But exactly because you didn't do anything...

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:52.460
Because you weren't involved in
the complications of human society...

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.050
That's what saved me.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.430
You were my first true friend.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.680
As a friend, let me warn you about one thing.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.020
What is it?

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:06.890
You're not like me. You're still young.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:12.900
You can't believe in a fake blue
and delude yourself it's the real thing.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:13.570
Blue?

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:17.320
The symbol of happiness.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.580
How can I tell the difference between
a fake blue and the real blue?

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.910
Be with someone.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.410
That's all it takes.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:29.960
Laughing with other people by your
side is what you can call happiness.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.500
You have nothing to worry about then.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:36.210
I actually consider the two
I came here with my true friends.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:38.470
I'm glad, then.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:43.680
There's no volume 407.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:47.890
I'm sure the previous notebooks are stored somewhere else.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.900
What is this script?

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:53.270
"The truth", according to the old man.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.530
Oh, there was already someone here.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:58.400
Hello, it's been a while.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.950
I believe you're from the Bureau?

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:03.490
And you're... I know you.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.450
Was it Asai?

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.870
I have some bad news for you.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.420
I'd rather not hear it, if possible.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:14.670
Entry to this office is prohibited for civilians.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.130
Even inside a dream?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:22.180
I asked for this building to be possible
to enter at this hour so that I could come here.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:25.560
What unbelievable coincidence
that you managed to wander in here.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:30.480
There're no copies of the Script earlier
than volume 852 in this room.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.810
Did the Bureau collect them?

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.820
Is that something you should know?

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.570
No, I don't mind if you pretend I never asked.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.150
I'm joking.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:44.870
These are the ones that man wrote
after he entered the dream world.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:48.870
Everything written before that
is being stored by the Bureau.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.330
I see.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:53.000
If we're not allowed to be here, we'll leave.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.040
I'm sorry we're driving you out.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:56.880
Excuse us.

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.630
Oh, actually.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:00.590
What is it?

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:01.720
Say, Asai.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:06.640
Your task was to spot the differences between
the dream world and the reality, wasn't it?

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:07.970
Yes, that's true.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:13.440
How come you are in this place, then?

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:18.530
We brought a friend here,
the girl sitting in the living room.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:20.990
I see. One more thing...

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:24.530
Don't you think the existence of
the Script could cause you despair?

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:26.200
I'm not sure.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.540
To be honest, I still can't believe it.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:38.800
Did Asai lie, I wonder?

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.090
Only his last words were a lie.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.300
Last words?

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.260
"To be honest, I still can't believe it."

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:48.810
These are the only words that appeared in red.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.390
He's accepted the existence of the Script.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.730
Oh, I see.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.020
His visit here is a problem.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:58.190
That goes for everyone.

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.490
Actually, you're not allowed to be here either.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.400
Civilians are forbidden from entry.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.910
Thought so.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:10.040
Asai Kei being here is a bigger problem
than other people would be.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.040
He won't forget what he read of the Script.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:17.790
The Bureau cannot allow the contents
of the Script to be leaked out.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.750
It's not that much of a problem.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.380
One little knife into his heart

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.390
and we can be sure no information will leak.

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:30.140
Do you think such a thing would be allowed?

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.310
I'm joking.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:35.770
There's someone behind Asai.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:38.480
There's no way he found this place by accident.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:41.020
I need reliable information.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:43.570
We'll need to question him.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:44.740
Why?

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.360
He's a nuisance.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:48.870
His ability is a huge nuisance.

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:51.370
He can't do anything, but he's an eyesore.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:55.080
If possible, I'd really like to get rid of him.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.500
Next Episode

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:00.210
Ability users are supposed to hate their abilities.

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:01.880
You should just forget about me and live on.

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:06.420
I strongly believe my sense of
what is right is better than yours.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:08.470
You have two selves that contradict each other.

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.390
Why do you hate me?

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:21.400
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.610
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:33.870
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:43.460
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:47.920
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:50.300
You get lost while searching for

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:54.180
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:54.180 --> 00:22:57.100
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:00.520
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:03.150
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:06.190
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:07.490
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:09.360
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:12.990
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:15.490
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:17.250
If it were so simple to just

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:20.250
Lock your own heart

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:23.380
How lovely life would be

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:28.630
But I believe you have the key

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:34.970
To let my soul be free
